## Minimize the pop-up, and the Call helper (release 43)

1. The line at the top right of a call minimizes it to a small chip at the bottom of the page: the caller''s name and the call''s timer. A click anywhere outside the panel, or Esc, minimizes it too; nothing is closed by accident. Press the chip to open the call again. The cross still closes a call in this browser, and a new call always opens by itself.
2. Inside each call, the **Call helper** is for new hires: **Say** (the greeting, with the staff member''s first name and the caller''s name and booking when known), a button for each situation with 3 to 6 short steps and links to the right page of their portal, and **Search the quick answers**. **Hide** puts it away in that browser.
3. You write all of it in **Settings** > **Call helper** (see Settings). **Edit** on the helper takes you there.

