4. To add your number as a sign-in, use **Profile** > **Sign-in** > **Add and verify my phone number**. No code after a minute? Press **Resend the code**, or **Save it without a code**: calls still ring it, but you sign in with your email until it is verified.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Customer service and Sales answer texts to the CarmaCars number in the same place as live chat. Every call and text is kept with the renter, owner or lead it belongs to.</p><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-answer-a-text" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer a text</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> tab, and press <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b>. Unread texts and missed calls are counted on each number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a number: calls and texts in order, and beside them who it is, with their bookings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write the text and press <b class="gd-ui">Send text</b>. It goes from the CarmaCars number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Suggest a reply</b> writes a draft into the box. Read it and change it: it is never sent until you press Send text.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-unknown-callers" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unknown callers</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Unknown callers</b>. Type the name if they told you and press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b>, or find the renter and press <b class="gd-ui">Link to</b> their name.</p><p class="gd-p">Quo&#39;s contacts follow the site: everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, added or updated within about five minutes. Change a name or number on the site, not in Quo: the site&#39;s version is sent again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-missed-calls" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missed calls</h2><p class="gd-p">A missed call gives you the task &quot;Missed call from ...&quot; when you have Live chat or Texts and calls open; otherwise it waits in the customer service queue. Call back with the Call button, or text, then mark the task done. Quo itself texts the caller back, so do not send the same message again.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A number that texted STOP gets no texts from us, booking texts included, until they text START. Prices go in a quote, never in a text from memory.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-email-text-or-both" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email, text or both</h2><p class="gd-p">Each renter and owner chooses how we reach them. Their page in Admin shows it under How we reach them; ask an Admin, or change it there if you can open the page. Texts need a phone they verified with a code. Your own choice is on your Profile, under Messages.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-call-and-text-buttons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and Text buttons</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Call and Text button in the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map&#39;s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person&#39;s conversation under <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b> (customer service and Sales); press <b class="gd-ui">Open the conversation</b> to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo&#39;s desktop app is your computer&#39;s calling app, tick <b class="gd-ui">On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app</b> once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An Admin can switch the buttons back to the phone&#39;s own apps in Program settings. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-who-is-calling-the-caller-pop-up-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service: when someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every page of your portal (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (<b class="gd-ui">overdue</b> when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a request, an offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what the call was about in <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b>. It is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the renter&#39;s page</b> opens their record. If it is outside your window, opening it from their call is logged as an opening for 24 hours with the reason Incoming call, as <b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b> is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An unknown number shows <b class="gd-ui">Unknown caller</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b> to keep it as a phone lead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press the line at the top right of the call to minimize it: it becomes a small chip at the bottom of the page with the caller&#39;s name and the call&#39;s timer. Clicking anywhere outside the panel, or pressing Esc, minimizes it too. Press the chip to open the call again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. A new call always opens by itself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-call-helper-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call helper (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">Inside every call on the pop-up, the <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> tells you what to say and do. It is made for your first weeks; press <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b> when you no longer need it (<b class="gd-ui">Show</b> brings it back).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Say</b>: the greeting to read out, with your first name, and the caller&#39;s name and booking when we know them. Start every call with it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">What is the call about?</b> Press the button that fits: New booking or price question, Change or extend a booking, Running late or late return, Pick-up and delivery, Deposit and payments, Insurance and protection, Accident or damage, Complaint, Owner wants to list a car, or Job applicant. You get 3 to 6 short steps. Words in bold quotes are what to say; a link opens the right page of your portal. <b class="gd-ui">All situations</b> goes back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Search the quick answers</b>: type a word (deposit, late, cancel, km) for the short answer to the questions callers ask most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The amounts, days and percentages in the steps and answers come from the settings, so they are always the ones in force. Never quote a price from memory: the offer screen works it out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Always finish with <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An Admin writes the greetings, the steps and the answers. Something wrong or missing? Tell an Admin: they change it in Settings and you see it on the next call.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s record (<b class="gd-ui">Find a renter</b>, then Open) has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and the notes are in its Activity log (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>), newest first, each with the date and time, who wrote it and their role. Add a note for every situation: what they asked, what you told them, what happens next. Notes cannot be changed or removed by staff, so write a new note to correct one; an Admin can remove a note with a reason. The notes also show on the caller pop-up and on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-lanes-the-call-button-and-hidden-numbers-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lanes, the Call button and hidden numbers (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each conversation has a lane: <b class="gd-ui">Fleet</b> for a car on rent, or a pickup, return, delivery or collection within a day; <b class="gd-ui">Customer service</b> for the rest. The inbox has a tab for each. The caller pop-up rings for Fleet first on Fleet&#39;s calls; customer service gets them when no Fleet staff member is on duty or nobody answered within 20 seconds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> rings your own phone first (the cell number in your profile). Answer it and we connect the customer, who sees the CarmaCars number. The call is noted on their history with its length. Until calling from the site is set up, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo as before and says why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sales sees customer numbers hidden, like (647) •••-••00. Use <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> on the page: the number is found on our side. Search by phone still works.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calling-from-the-site-your-mobile-release-40" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calling from the site: your mobile (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a lead, a renter, a request or a booking rings your own mobile first, then connects the person. They see the CarmaCars number, never yours. Sales see the number hidden and call this way only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The first time, with no mobile on your profile, a small window asks <b class="gd-ui">Your mobile number</b>. Type your Canadian or US mobile (10 digits, for example (647) 555-0123) and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and call</b>. No code is texted: it is saved to your profile and the call starts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your phone rings. Answer it: you hear &quot;CarmaCars call. Connecting you now.&quot; and the person&#39;s phone rings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A call that cannot start says why in the same window, with <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b>. Calling from the site not set up: ask customer service or an Admin to call, and tell an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To add your number as a sign-in, use <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sign-in</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add and verify my phone number</b>. No code after a minute? Press <b class="gd-ui">Resend the code</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Save it without a code</b>: calls still ring it, but you sign in with your email until it is verified.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
-- GUIDES 2721 END
